From 4e857b2a6964c4b63dd6521f00062077bbdd663d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "zhaoming.274" <zhaoming.274@bytedance.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 22:47:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bit-semantics migration across AI evaluators and garbage
 row generation

Inverted TetrisMap row semantics from 1=occupied to 1=empty in a1e4ac6, but several AI evaluators, danger detectors and garbage row generators still followed the old semantics. This commit completes the migration so that the branch matches master behaviour while exploiting the new representation for cheaper bit math.

Key changes vs master:

- TetrisContext now caches a row mask (line value with width-bits set) and exposes row_mask() so callers do not need to derive it from full() every time. TetrisMap auto-clears on (w,h) construction so callers no longer need an explicit clear() after construction; the empty board representation is established once and uses the new 1=empty semantics.
- All AI evaluators (ai_ax, ai_tag, ai_zzz Attack/Dig/TOJ/TOJ_PC/TOJ_v08/Botris/Botris_PC/C2, ai_misaka) re-derive holes, row transitions, well shapes and clear width using the inverted bits. Hot loops introduce a single inv_row = ~map.row[y] & row_mask_ to share the BMI ANDN result across all per-row metrics.
- map_danger_data_ stores 1=occupied bits, so map_in_danger_ becomes a single ANDN against map.row, matching what the BMI instruction set fuses.
- Garbage row generation in the_ai_games, cmd_tris, pso and ppt_pso now writes 1 << x for the hole column instead of full() & ~(1<<x), aligning with the convention already used in botris.cpp.
- Added a .clang-format covering Allman braces, 4-space indent, right pointer alignment and ColumnLimit 0 to lock in the existing style; only files touched by this commit have been reformatted.

Co-Authored-By: Aime <aime@bytedance.com>
Change-Id: Ic0885a591af4f64c9f0462a9002c36e679af50cd
